    "q-124349": {
      "dom_id": "step-q124349",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14274717/assets/0da125535534cbd50b96cb280cf8b8a4b58653a344c8699d7b732ec73cc3b2ce.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the closed path along a right triangle, traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above.",
      "worked_solution": "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, the initial and terminal points are the same (since the path is closed and is traversed only once). Therefore, ${y}_{1}={y}_{2},$ and we have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
